    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The trough behavior is automatic; there is no activation key. To test the currently installed build: (1) use the owned/current horse with stamina core below 75%; (2) dismount and make sure it is not hitched, attached, fleeing, injured, in combat, or otherwise busy; (3) leave it beside an actual horse trough; (4) walk 6-80 m away; and (5) leave the horse still for 15 seconds. It should take the authored trough-drinking scenario and restore the stamina core gradually. Approaching, whistling, mounting, danger, or another busy state interrupts it. The hay path has the same automatic idle/need behavior near the validated loose-hay sources. This implementation is already present in the hash-verified installed combined ASI (AC952387AA9932EFD4AA43C580D4369F0534537A01B0196A529BBC88519551D9), so this needs in-game confirmation rather than more implementation.",
